  "senderName": "NWS Baltimore MD/Washington DC",
  "headline": "Tornado Warning issued July 21 at 6:29PM EDT until July 21 at 6:45PM EDT by NWS Baltimore MD/Washington DC",
  "description": "At 629 PM EDT, a confirmed large and extremely dangerous tornado was\nlocated near Star Tannery, or 10 miles west of Winchester, moving\neast at 20 mph.\n\nThis is a PARTICULARLY DANGEROUS SITUATION. TAKE COVER NOW!\n\nHAZARD...Damaging tornado.\n\nSOURCE...Radar confirmed tornado.\n\nIMPACT...You are in a life-threatening situation. Flying debris may\nbe deadly to those caught without shelter. Mobile homes\nwill be destroyed. Considerable damage to homes,\nbusinesses, and vehicles is likely and complete destruction\nis possible.\n\nLocations impacted include...\nHigh View Manor and Wilde Acres.",
  "instruction": "To repeat, a tornado is on the ground. To protect your life, TAKE\nCOVER NOW! Move to a basement or an interior room on the lowest\nfloor of a sturdy building. Avoid windows. If you are outdoors, in a\nmobile home, or in a vehicle, move to the closest substantial\nshelter and protect yourself from flying debris.",
